>>
endobj
157 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 126 0 R
/E (Mango farming often suffers yield losses due to leaf diseases and nutrient deficiencies, usually detected only after serious damage. Early and automated detection can help farmers act promptly, reduce losses, and improve crop quality. This project proposes a machine learning-based system using image processing to detect and classify diseases and nutrient deficiencies in mango leaves. Leaf images are pre-processed through resizing, normalization, noise reduction, and colour space conversion to manage variations in lighting and field conditions. Segmentation separates leaves from the background, and key features including colour histograms, texture features \(GLCM and LBP\), and shape descriptors are extracted. These features are analysed with machine learning algorithms such as Random Forest, SVM, and KNN for accurate classification. Later, deep learning models like DenseNet-121 with transfer learning will be explored. Unlike manual diagnosis, this approach is faster, reliable, and requires no expert knowledge, offering farmers a cost-effective and efficient tool for early detection.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
